// endpoint_update_rollouts.proto — UpdateRollouts: hold or release the
// runtime's ROLLOUTS. RUNTIME section. A rollout is the redeploy a landing in
// the daemon's own checkout triggers: rebuilding and restarting the running
// daemon, shims and editor code onto what landed.
//
// HOLDING stops those redeploys daemon-wide while merges keep running and
// landing exactly as they do: for an operator running a hand-deployed build (a
// profiling build) that a landing would otherwise replace. DURABLE: a hold
// survives a daemon restart and a handover until it is released.
//
// RELEASING DEPLOYS WHAT LANDED. Releasing ends the hold and, when the daemon's
// checkout holds landings the running build does not carry, rolls them out at
// once, so no landing is left undeployed by a hold.

